The question is asking you to parse the C# code to find comments starting with "@@@", and then convert those comments into C# code that uses the "Debug.Assert" statement. 

Here's a high-level overview of how you might achieve that:

1) Programmatically read the C# code using a C# parsing library.

2) Then, for each method, for each line of code:
   a) If the line is a comment starting with "@@@", remove the "@@@" and replace it with "Debug.Assert(".
   b) If the line has a variable name, check if that variable name is used as a value in the line. If it is, append ", Message=\"" and the variable name followed by "\"" to construct the debug.assert statement.

Here's an example code of how you can approach this with a string manipulation:

```cs
using System;
using System.Text.RegularExpressions;

class Program 
{
   public static string replaceComment(String comment)
   {
        string cleanedUpComment = Regex.Replace(comment, @"\$old|\$new", "");
        cleanedUpComment = "Debug.Assert(" + cleanedUpComment + ");";
        return cleanedUpComment;
   }

   public static void Main() 
   {
       string comment = "@@@ the return value is index of x in new array";
       string output = replaceComment(comment);
       Console.WriteLine(output);
   }
}
```
